  "doc": {
    "controller": "Cemu automatically loads controllerProfiles/controller0.xml for player one before CafeSystem initialization. The 0_ prefix is Cemu's duplicate-GUID index followed by SDL_JoystickGetGUIDString's 32 lowercase hexadecimal digits. Mapping ids are VPAD ButtonId values; button ids are the pinned 2.6 SDL_GameControllerButton values and Controller.h synthetic axis values. The Semu source build ignores per-title controller overrides so this generated profile remains authoritative.",
    "display": "open_pad=false leaves one primary game window. Ctrl+Tab changes whether that main window presents TV or GamePad output; the separate pad window remains closed. Notification Position 0 is ScreenPosition::kDisabled, so Cemu draws no notification box (shader compiles, friends, controllers, warnings) over the game.",
    "audio": "The Wii U TV plays through Cubeb on the default output device, in stereo, at unity gain like every other emulator Semu runs. Cemu a6fb0a4 reads <Audio> with api 0 (DirectSound) and an empty TVDevice when the block is missing (CemuConfig.cpp:271-290), and an empty device opens no TV stream at all (IAudioAPI.cpp:116-117), so every Wii U game was silent; DirectSound and XAudio exist only on Windows (IAudioAPI.cpp:79-88). api 3 is IAudioAPI::Cubeb (IAudioAPI.h:33-41), whose device list always starts with the identifier default, Cubeb's default output (devid null, CubebAPI.cpp:184-196), which on Linux is PulseAudio or PipeWire's pulse server; TVChannels 1 is kStereo (CemuConfig.h:79-84) and TVVolume 100 is cubeb_stream_set_volume 1.0. The GamePad speaker keeps Cemu's own default, no device and volume 0 (CemuConfig.h:483-484), so a game that mirrors its mix to the pad is not heard twice; the microphone has no device and stays off (mic.cpp:146-172). The set must be whole: a TVDevice with an unavailable api makes AXOut_init exit (IAudioAPI.cpp:119-128, ax_out.cpp:403-413).",
    "storage": "The profile pins only input, UI and audio settings. emulator.json owns the XDG and -m paths that keep normal Wii U title saves inside the isolated MLC root.",
    "actions": "Native rows are fail-closed invariants checked against steamdeck.skm before emission. Unsupported rows document shared Semu actions that this exact upstream release cannot consume.",
    "players": "One controller<N>.xml per player with a pad (for_each players): player 1 is the Wii U GamePad (controller0.xml), players 2 to 4 Wii U Pro Controllers (controller1-3.xml, ProController::ButtonId 1-25: A, B, X, Y, L, R, ZL, ZR, Plus, Minus, Home, the d-pad, the stick clicks and the eight stick directions, Cemu v2.6 src/input/emulated/ProController.h) on the same SDL button ids as the GamePad. Each uuid is Cemu's <same-GUID index>_<SDL GUID> from the launch's roster; player 1 on the first pad keeps the target's device_identities uuid. Cemu loads controller<N>.xml for player N at boot (InputManager.cpp:75-81)."
  },
  "native_shortcuts": {
    "source": "cemu a6fb0a4 src/gui/MainWindow.cpp:1425-1453",
    "fallback": true,
    "why": "Cemu 2.6 has no configurable hotkeys; its window handles a few keys itself, listed under fixed.",
    "defaults": [],
    "fixed": [
      {
        "key": "Esc",
        "consumer": "MainWindow::OnKeyUp leaves fullscreen",
        "accepted": "Cemu cannot unbind it. No Steam Input binding sends Esc (the radial and the hotkey set use Semu chords only), so only a desktop keyboard's own Esc reaches it, as in any Cemu."
      },
      {
        "key": "Alt+Enter",
        "consumer": "MainWindow::OnKeyUp toggles fullscreen"
      },
      {
        "key": "F11",
        "consumer": "MainWindow::OnKeyUp toggles fullscreen"
      },
      {
        "key": "F12",
        "consumer": "MainWindow::OnKeyUp takes a screenshot"
      },
      {
        "key": "Alt+F4",
        "action": "app.quit",
        "consumer": "MainWindow::OnKeyDown closes Cemu"
      },
      {
        "key": "Ctrl+Q",
        "action": "app.quit",
        "consumer": "MainWindow::OnKeyDown closes Cemu (CmdDown is Ctrl outside macOS)"
      }
    ]
  }
}
